      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Other GPIO helpers in this script (`gpio()` on line 436 and `gpio_chip_exists()` on line 444) encapsulate the `USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API` check inside the helper layer, and `_gpio_new()` treats legacy-only operations (`export`, `unexport`, `in`, `out`) as no-ops so `flash_fp_mcu_board()` can invoke GPIO helpers unconditionally.\n\nPlease move the `USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API` guard into `warn_gpio()` (lines 454–469) so that:\n1. `USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API` remains encapsulated in the GPIO helper layer and any caller of `warn_gpio()` is protected from invoking `gpioget` under the character-device API.\n2. The behavior can be directly unit-tested in `util/flash_fp_mcu_test.sh` (which is cited in `TEST\u003d` but currently has no test case covering `warn_gpio` with `USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API\u003d0` vs. `USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API\u003d1`).\n\nIn `util/flash_fp_mcu`:\n```bash\n# Usage: warn_gpio \u003csignal\u003e \u003cexpected_value\u003e \u003cmsg\u003e\nwarn_gpio() {\n  # Only check GPIO state via sysfs legacy API. With the character-device GPIO\n  # API, gpioset either holds the line open (blocking gpioget) or gpioget\n  # reconfigures the line as input (clobbering the output driven on BOOT0/NRST).\n  if [[ \"${USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API}\" -ne 1 ]]; then\n    return 0\n  fi\n\n  local signal\u003d$1\n  local expected_value\u003d$2\n  local msg\u003d$3\n\n  local value\n  if ! value\u003d\"$(gpio get \"${signal}\")\"; then\n    echo \"Error fetching gpio value ${signal}\" \u003e\u00262\n    exit \"${EXIT_RUNTIME}\"\n  fi\n\n  if [[ \"${value}\" !\u003d \"${expected_value}\" ]]; then\n    echo \"${msg}\" \u003e\u00262\n    return 1\n  fi\n}\n```\n\nAnd at the call site in `flash_fp_mcu_board()`:\n```bash\n  # We do not expect the drivers to change the pin state when binding.\n  # If you receive this warning, the driver needs to be fixed on this board\n  # and this flash attempt will probably fail.\n  warn_gpio \"${gpio_boot0}\" 1 \\\n    \"WARNING: One of the drivers changed BOOT0 pin state on bind attempt.\"\n  warn_gpio \"${gpio_nrst}\" 0 \\\n    \"WARNING: One of the drivers changed NRST pin state on bind attempt.\"\n```\n\nThen add unit tests in `util/flash_fp_mcu_test.sh` covering both `USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API\u003d0` and `USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API\u003d1`:\n```bash\n# 7. warn_gpio only queries GPIO state when USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API\u003d1\n(\n  USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API\u003d0\n  gpio_called\u003d0\n  gpio() { gpio_called\u003d1; }\n  warn_gpio \"gpiochip0:46\" 1 \"unexpected warning\"\n  assert_eq \"0\" \"${gpio_called}\" \"warn_gpio skipped when USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API\u003d0\"\n)\n(\n  USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API\u003d1\n  gpio() { echo \"1\"; }\n  warn_gpio \"46\" 1 \"unexpected warning\"\n)\n(\n  USE_LEGACY_GPIO_API\u003d1\n  gpio() { echo \"0\"; }\n  ret\u003d0\n  err\u003d\"$(warn_gpio \"46\" 1 \"pin state changed\" 2\u003e\u00261)\" || ret\u003d$?\n  assert_eq \"1\" \"${ret}\" \"warn_gpio returns 1 on mismatch\"\n  assert_eq \"pin state changed\" \"${err}\" \"warn_gpio prints warning on mismatch\"\n)\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/a44da871-b2dc-4da4-9de8-82a48e1be1b1)",
